<id/13/1363/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Chromite (Chromic Iron)"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q107172> ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_metallic_ores/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "an important mineral. The green oxide furnishes a valuable colour for oil-painting, enamel, and porcelain. Chrome iron ore forms the basis of many of the coloured preparations of chrome used in dyeing, and for the production of chromate of potash. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 101]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_metallic_ores; processing_state=raw_ore): Ore/concentrate heading (chromite / chromate of iron in tons; metal 'contained in ore, matte, regulus'; pyrites); belongs with Metallic Ores & Concentrates like its sibling headings. Layer-1 observations: 13 rows, 1895–1901. Series: CSP_Canadian_Exports_BlankSeries (inferred, series not printed) ×10. Units: Tons ×13. Top routes: Canada → United States ×3; Canada → All Countries ×2; Ontario → All Countries ×2; Quebec → All Countries ×2."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "1363" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Chromite (Chromic Iron)"@en ;
